% XSB write_term OPTIONS WITNESS xwr02 (hq_packages 2026-10-29, prolog_tests/wttest, pip_write_term): ignore_ops writes lists as .(a,.(b,[])), portable keeps lists and braces, integer_base and
% integer_prefix and radix write 0xff, 16'ff, 8'377, 0o173, a code list of printable codes is written as a double-quoted string, max_depth counts list elements as XSB does, an invalid option is a
% domain_error(write_option, Option). The ref is XSB 5.0.0 own output (xsb_bin, gentest protocol), never SCRIP output.
t(L, G) :- write(L), write(' = '), ( catch(G, E, (E = error(Ex,_), write(caught(Ex)))) -> true ; write(failed) ), nl.
